{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GZW9fQzNz1kAYQiBg8PZ5G","type":"tool_result","content":"The release notes say that inline projects inherit the root config by default. The change is listed under breaking changes: \"Inline projects extend the root config by default\" (#10750).\n\nA related fix adds a warning for a side effect of that inheritance. The notes mention a warning \"if inline project has duplicate plugins due to unexpected `extends: true`\" (#11120). So if a project's `extends: true` pulls in plugins the project also declares, Vitest now warns about the duplicates."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b8bf498-03fb-49ac-93de-233541408eb7","uuid":"adcf23a8-6706-47f3-8160-f405402efc64","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:43.599Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":451732,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The release notes say that inline projects inherit the root config by default. The change is listed under breaking changes: \"Inline projects extend the root config by default\" (#10750).\n\nA related fix adds a warning for a side effect of that inheritance. The notes mention a warning \"if inline project has duplicate plugins due to unexpected `extends: true`\" (#11120). So if a project's `extends: true` pulls in plugins the project also declares, Vitest now warns about the duplicates.","durationMs":3069,"url":"https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GZW9fQzNz1kAYQiBg8PZ5G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnUeuqKqtVbC3tog8G3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It depends on your Vitest version. In Vitest 5, you don't need it. Inline projects in `test.projects` inherit the root config by default, and the v5.0.0 release notes list this as a breaking change (#10750). In Vitest 4 and earlier, you still need `extends: true` on each inline project.\n\nIf you're on Vitest 5 and still have `extends: true` in your config, consider removing it. It can bring in plugins a second time, and Vitest 5 now warns about duplicate plugins in inline projects.\n\nSource: [Vitest v5.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":5395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":445},"output_tokens":219,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b8bf498-03fb-49ac-93de-233541408eb7","uuid":"72895fa0-0985-4050-ba3b-1909bae8d6bb","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:46.496Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnUefCgJ3SdyxETrUvu"}
